<title>USA: Intel trades at 81-1/2 after hours.</title>
<headline>Intel trades at 81-1/2 after hours.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Intel Corp traded at 81-1/2 in after-hours trade on Tuesday, up more than half a point from an unofficial close of 80-29/32, traders said.</p>
<p>Shares in the semiconductor manufacturer rose after the company reported after the close of regular trade that second quarter earnings rose to $0.92 per share from $0.59 for the year-ago period.</p>
<p>According to First Call, analysts had forecast that Intel's closely watched earnings performance would come in at $0.90 per share.</p>
</text>
